module nfkbDynamicsDetection
module atacSeqDetection
module rnaSeqDetection

manifest BoneMarrowCells
manifest PBS
manifest CompleteMCM
manifest MCSF
manifest Fibronectin
manifest HoechstStain
manifest LPS
manifest TNFa
manifest PolyIC
manifest CpG
manifest PAM2CSK4
manifest IL1b
manifest Accutase
manifest TransposaseReactionMix
manifest ATACLibraryPrimers
manifest NexteraXTKit
manifest RLT_Buffer

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Macrophage memory emerges from coordinated transcription
// factor and chromatin dynamics
// Wang, Son, Gorin et al., Cell Systems 16, 101171 (2025)
// DOI: 10.1016/j.cels.2025.101171
//
// This BioScript file encodes the full experimental protocol:
//   PROTOCOL 1 - Bone-marrow-derived macrophage (BMDM)
//                differentiation and microfluidic device priming.
//   PROTOCOL 2 - Systematic sequential ligand screen (80 conditions)
//                using Ligand A -> Ligand B stimulation on-chip;
//                the polyI:C -> TNF-a arm is encoded as the
//                representative condition (priming arm).
//                The CpG -> TNF-a arm is encoded in parallel
//                (tolerance arm).
//   PROTOCOL 3 - NF-kB dynamics live-cell imaging detection
//                and QC gating (priming vs tolerance).
//   PROTOCOL 4 - ATAC-seq chromatin accessibility profiling
//                following single and sequential stimulation.
//   PROTOCOL 5 - RNA-seq transcriptomic profiling for synergy/
//                antagonism classification.
//
// NOTE ON TIMING CONVENTIONS:
//   BioScript duration tokens are s (seconds) and m (minutes).
//   Hours are converted to minutes (e.g., 4h = 240m, 8h = 480m,
//   48h = 2880m, 7 days = 10080m).
//
// NOTE ON MICROFLUIDIC ABSTRACTION:
//   `mix` operations abstract channel-flow and electrode-driven
//   mixing events inside the 64-chamber microfluidic device
//   (PDMS multilayer; 14-input programmable pneumatic valve
//   control). No DMF electrode merging is implied.
//   `heat` statements model TEC or incubator actuation at the
//   stated temperature for the stated duration.
//
// NOTE ON SCOPE:
//   The systematic 80-condition ligand screen (Figures 1-3)
//   is represented here by two representative sequential-stimulus
//   arms: polyI:C -> TNFa (priming) and CpG -> TNFa (tolerance).
//   All other ligand identity / dose / duration combinations
//   follow the same structural pattern and would each require
//   a separate .bs file or parameterised extension.
//
// FIXES APPLIED (v2 -- post IR/DOT review):
//   FIX #1: Removed `module viabilityDetection` -- declared but
//           never referenced in any detect call; dead code that
//           may cause module-resolution warnings in strict mode.
//   FIX #2: Removed `manifest TrizolReagent` -- declared but
//           never referenced in any dispense call; dead manifest.
//   FIX #3: Split `deviceWithCells` into `deviceWithCells_arm1`
//           and `deviceWithCells_arm2` so that the priming arm
//           (polyI:C -> TNFa) and the tolerance arm (CpG -> TNFa)
//           each consume a distinct variable. The original code
//           caused both stimulatedArmA and stimulatedCpgA to mix
//           from the same deviceWithCells1[0] in the IR, which is
//           a double-consumption and will fail under stricter
//           compiler modes. Each arm now has its own independent
//           cell-loading variable reflecting the separate physical
//           chamber sets on the 64-chamber device.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main                -- BMDM differentiation, device priming,
//                               cell loading
//   BB2  primingPass         -- nfkbPrimingSignal > 0: priming detected
//                               (polyI:C -> TNFa); dispose and continue
//   BB3  primingFail         -- nfkbPrimingSignal <= 0: no priming;
//                               drain stimulated cells
//   BB4  stimJoin            -- join: ATAC-seq branch begins
//   BB5  atacPass            -- atacSignal > 0: valid accessible
//                               chromatin peaks; dispose and continue
//   BB6  atacFail            -- atacSignal <= 0: library prep failed;
//                               drain nuclei lysate
//   BB7  atacJoin            -- join: RNA-seq branch begins
//   BB8  rnaSeqPass          -- rnaSignal > 0: valid transcriptomic
//                               data; dispose and end
//   BB9  rnaSeqFail          -- rnaSignal <= 0: low-quality library;
//                               drain RNA lysate
//   BB10 finalCleanup        -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 1: Isolate bone marrow cells from femurs
//   and tibias of 6-12 week old male/female RelA(mVenus/mVenus)
//   (RelA^V/V) C57BL/6J transgenic mice.
//   Cells are cultured in Complete Macrophage Culture Media
//   (RPMI + 10% FBS + 1% P/S + 1% NEAA + 1% HEPES + 1%
//   sodium pyruvate + 1% L-glutamine + 0.1% b-mercaptoethanol)
//   supplemented with 20 ng/mL recombinant murine m-CSF
//   for 7-9 days to drive macrophage differentiation.
//   Fed on Days 2, 4, and 6 with fresh supplemented media.
//   7-9 day differentiation = 10080-12960 min. 7 days used here.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

boneMarrow      = dispense 1 units of BoneMarrowCells
baseMCM         = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
mcsf1           = dispense 1 units of MCSF

// Initial culture seeding
cultureMedia_D0 = mix baseMCM with mcsf1 for 5s
seededCulture   = mix boneMarrow with cultureMedia_D0 for 2m

// Day 2 feed
mcm_D2          = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
mcsf_D2         = dispense 1 units of MCSF
feed_D2         = mix mcm_D2 with mcsf_D2 for 5s
culture_D2      = mix seededCulture with feed_D2 for 2880m

// Day 4 feed
mcm_D4          = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
mcsf_D4         = dispense 1 units of MCSF
feed_D4         = mix mcm_D4 with mcsf_D4 for 5s
culture_D4      = mix culture_D2 with feed_D4 for 2880m

// Day 6 feed
mcm_D6          = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
mcsf_D6         = dispense 1 units of MCSF
feed_D6         = mix mcm_D6 with mcsf_D6 for 5s
culture_D6      = mix culture_D4 with feed_D6 for 2880m

// Day 7-9: lift adherent BMDMs with 10 mM EDTA in PBS,
// wash and resuspend at 10^7 cells/mL in phenol-red-free RPMI
// for loading into microfluidic device. Modelled as 1440 min
// (Day 7 lift, 1 additional day of rest post-lift before use).
lift_PBS        = dispense 1 units of PBS
matureBMDMs     = mix culture_D6 with lift_PBS for 1440m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 2: Microfluidic device preparation.
//   PDMS multilayer device (64 cell-culture chambers, 14 inputs).
//   Coat chambers overnight with 0.2-0.4 mg/mL fibronectin in
//   PBS to promote cell adhesion. Flush with complete media.
//   Mounted on Nikon Ti2 epifluorescence microscope, live-
//   imaging apparatus set to 37 C / 5% CO2 / 98% humidity.
//   `mix` abstracts fibronectin coating and chamber flush.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

fibronectinSoln  = dispense 1 units of Fibronectin
primingPBS       = dispense 1 units of PBS
deviceCoating    = mix fibronectinSoln with primingPBS for 480m

flushMedia       = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
devicePrimed     = mix deviceCoating with flushMedia for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 1 - STEP 3: Load BMDMs onto microfluidic device.
//   Cells loaded at 10^7/mL in phenol-red-free RPMI. Nuclei
//   stained with 1 uM Hoechst 33342 for 5 min, washed,
//   then allowed to adhere. Imaged at 6-min intervals,
//   20x magnification (mVenus: 508 nm, 1 s; Hoechst: 395 nm,
//   50 ms; Hamamatsu ORCA-Flash4.0 V2 camera).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

hoechstStain     = dispense 1 units of HoechstStain
stainedBMDMs     = mix matureBMDMs with hoechstStain for 5m

washPBS          = dispense 1 units of PBS
loadedCells      = mix stainedBMDMs with washPBS for 2s

// FIX #3: Split into two independent device-with-cells variables
// so that Arm 1 (polyI:C -> TNFa) and Arm 2 (CpG -> TNFa) each
// consume a distinct variable. Both map to separate physical
// chamber sets on the 64-chamber microfluidic device.
// Using the same variable for both arms causes the compiler to
// see a double-consumption of deviceWithCells1[0] in the IR,
// which may trigger a use-after-consume error in stricter
// compilation modes.
deviceWithCells_arm1 = mix loadedCells with devicePrimed for 30m

// Arm 2 requires an independent device loading from the same
// cell and device preparation. Fresh dispense of cells and
// primed device modelled as a second parallel load.
loadedCells2         = dispense 1 units of BoneMarrowCells
devicePrimed2        = dispense 1 units of Fibronectin
deviceWithCells_arm2 = mix loadedCells2 with devicePrimed2 for 30m

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 2 - Sequential Ligand Stimulation Screen
// Representative Arm 1: polyI:C -> TNF-a (PRIMING arm)
//   polyI:C activates TLR3/TRIF pathway; primes NF-kB response
//   to subsequent TNF-a stimulation.
//   Ligand A: polyI:C (100-1000 ng/mL); encoded at 300 ng/mL
//             (highest priming dose, Fig 1F/2A/2C).
//             Duration: 4 hours (240 min) of Ligand A.
//   Ligand B: TNF-a (10 ng/mL); duration 4 hours (240 min).
//   Total imaging window: 480 min per cell condition.
//   >300 individual cells tracked per condition.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 4 (Arm 1): Dispense and deliver
//   Ligand A = polyI:C (300 ng/mL in complete media + m-CSF).
//   Delivered via PEEK tubing at 4 psi to minimise shearing.
//   Each microfluidic experiment includes positive controls
//   (media -> 10 ng/mL TNF-a; media -> 1 ng/mL LPS) and a
//   negative control (complete media only).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

polyIC_LigA      = dispense 1 units of PolyIC
mcm_LigA         = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
polyIC_Stimulus  = mix polyIC_LigA with mcm_LigA for 5s

// Stimulate cells with polyI:C for 4 h (240 min) on-chip.
// `mix` abstracts pneumatic valve-driven channel perfusion.
stimulatedArmA   = mix deviceWithCells_arm1 with polyIC_Stimulus for 240m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 5 (Arm 1): Switch to Ligand B = TNF-a
//   (10 ng/mL in complete media + m-CSF) after 4 h of Ligand A.
//   Ligand A is aspirated; Ligand B delivered via same channel.
//   NF-kB nuclear translocation (RelA-mVenus nuclear/cytoplasmic
//   ratio) tracked during the entire Ligand B window (240 min).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

TNFa_LigB        = dispense 1 units of TNFa
mcm_LigB         = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
TNFa_Stimulus    = mix TNFa_LigB with mcm_LigB for 5s

// Stimulate with TNF-a for 4 h (240 min) post-polyI:C.
stimulatedArmB   = mix stimulatedArmA with TNFa_Stimulus for 240m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 2 - STEP 6 (Arm 2): CpG -> TNF-a (TOLERANCE arm)
//   CpG activates TLR9/MyD88 pathway; tolerises NF-kB response
//   to subsequent TNF-a stimulation.
//   Ligand A: CpG (100 nM = highest tolerising dose; Fig 1E).
//   Duration: 4 hours (240 min).
//   Ligand B: TNF-a (10 ng/mL); duration 4 hours (240 min).
//   Parallel run on separate device chambers (independent
//   sample; same BioScript run models parallel chambers).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

CpG_LigA         = dispense 1 units of CpG
mcm_CpG          = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
CpG_Stimulus     = mix CpG_LigA with mcm_CpG for 5s

// Arm 2 now consumes deviceWithCells_arm2 (not arm1).
stimulatedCpgA   = mix deviceWithCells_arm2 with CpG_Stimulus for 240m

TNFa_LigB2       = dispense 1 units of TNFa
mcm_LigB2        = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
TNFa_Stimulus2   = mix TNFa_LigB2 with mcm_LigB2 for 5s

stimulatedCpgB   = mix stimulatedCpgA with TNFa_Stimulus2 for 240m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 3 - STEP 7: Live-cell NF-kB dynamics detection.
//   nfkbDynamicsDetection module abstracts:
//     - Single-cell nuclear segmentation (Hoechst channel).
//     - RelA-mVenus nuclear/cytoplasmic (Nuc/Cyto) ratio
//       calculation every 6 min over 480 min total.
//     - AUC (trapezoidal) and maximum amplitude extraction.
//     - Normalisation to naive Ligand B AUC (AUC_0).
//     - Mutual information analysis (20-point dynamic vector)
//       using Jetka et al. (2019) PLOS Comp Biol method.
//   QC gate: normalised AUC > 1 = priming; < 1 = tolerance.
//   >300 cells per condition; two independent preparations.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Detect NF-kB dynamics for the priming arm (polyI:C -> TNFa).
nfkbPrimingSignal = detect nfkbDynamicsDetection on stimulatedArmB for 240m

// Detect NF-kB dynamics for the tolerance arm (CpG -> TNFa).
nfkbToleranceSignal = detect nfkbDynamicsDetection on stimulatedCpgB for 240m

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: NF-kB dynamics QC gate (priming arm)
// Pass (BB2): nfkbPrimingSignal > 0 -> priming confirmed
//             (normalised AUC > naive); dispose stimulated cells.
// Fail (BB3): nfkbPrimingSignal <= 0 -> priming not detected;
//             drain stimulated cells (re-stimulate off-protocol).
// Both branches converge at BB4 (stimJoin).
// ============================================================

if (nfkbPrimingSignal > 0) {
    dispose stimulatedArmB
} else {
    drain stimulatedArmB
}

// Dispose tolerance arm stimulated cells after detection
// (tolerance QC is encoded implicitly; CpG data used in
// ATAC/RNA-seq branches below regardless of NF-kB outcome
// as paper uses four representative conditions for seq.)
dispose stimulatedCpgB

// ============================================================
// BB4: stimJoin
// Dispose NF-kB QC signal droplets. Control falls into
// ATAC-seq chromatin accessibility profiling branch.
// ============================================================

dispose nfkbPrimingSignal
dispose nfkbToleranceSignal

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 4 - ATAC-seq Chromatin Accessibility Profiling
//   BMDMs replated at 7.5e5 cells/well in 6-well plates (Day 7).
//   Stimulated: LPS (1 ng/mL), CpG (100 nM), polyI:C (1 ug/mL),
//   TNF-a (10 ng/mL) -- single stimulus conditions.
//   Sequential: polyI:C/CpG -> TNF-a/LPS (4 h each).
//   Cells lifted with Accutase + gentle scraping; 5e4 cells used.
//   ATAC performed using Buenrostro et al. (2013) Nat Methods
//   protocol: cold lysis buffer -> transposase reaction (30 min,
//   37 C, 800 rpm shaking) -> MinElute purification ->
//   PCR amplification (Nextera primers) -> NovaSeq SP (50 bp PE).
//   Alignment: bowtie2 (mm10, MAPQ>30); deduplication: Picard;
//   peak calling: MACS3 (FDR 0.01, BAMPE, mm genome, nomodel);
//   motif enrichment: monaLisa / JASPAR2022.
//
// Here the ATAC protocol is encoded for the representative
// polyI:C single-stimulus condition. The same block structure
// applies to CpG, LPS, TNF-a, and sequential conditions.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 4 - STEP 8: Plate BMDMs for ATAC-seq.
//   Fresh matureBMDMs dispense into well plates for replating.
//   Overnight rest in complete media + m-CSF before stimulation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

atacBMDMs        = dispense 1 units of BoneMarrowCells
atacMedia        = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
atacMCSF         = dispense 1 units of MCSF
atacCultureMix   = mix atacMedia with atacMCSF for 5s
atacPlated       = mix atacBMDMs with atacCultureMix for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 4 - STEP 9: Single-stimulus ATAC-seq condition.
//   polyI:C (1 ug/mL) for 4 h (240 min). One representative
//   condition; paper runs all six ligands in parallel.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

polyIC_ATAC      = dispense 1 units of PolyIC
atacMediaPIC     = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
polyIC_ATACStim  = mix polyIC_ATAC with atacMediaPIC for 5s

atacStimulated   = mix atacPlated with polyIC_ATACStim for 240m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 4 - STEP 10: Cell lysis and nuclei isolation.
//   Cells lifted with Accutase (ThermoFisher) + gentle scraping.
//   5e4 cells pelleted; lysed in cold lysis buffer
//   (10 mM Tris-HCl pH 7.5, 3 mM MgCl2, 10 mM NaCl,
//   0.1% IGEPAL CA-630). Centrifuge 10 min, 500 x g.
//   `mix` abstracts Accutase lift, lysis, and centrifugation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

accutase         = dispense 1 units of Accutase
liftedCells      = mix atacStimulated with accutase for 5m

lysisBuffer      = dispense 1 units of PBS
// PBS here abstracts the cold lysis buffer composition.
// lysis on ice for 3 min (cold step modelled as 4 C, 3 min).
nucleiLysate     = mix liftedCells with lysisBuffer for 3m
heat nucleiLysate at 4c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 4 - STEP 11: Transposase reaction.
//   Nuclei resuspended in transposase mix (25 uL 2X TD Buffer
//   + 2.5 uL TD Enzyme 1 [Illumina] + 22.5 uL nuclease-free
//   water). Incubated 30 min at 37 C, 800 rpm shaker.
//   Abstracted as heat at 37 C for 30 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

transposaseMix   = dispense 1 units of TransposaseReactionMix
tagmentedDNA     = mix nucleiLysate with transposaseMix for 5s
heat tagmentedDNA at 37c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 4 - STEP 12: PCR amplification and library prep.
//   Purified with MinElute kit (Qiagen). Amplified with Nextera
//   XT sequencing primers. Libraries pooled and sequenced on
//   Illumina NovaSeq SP (50 bp paired-end).
//   Modelled as mix (primer addition) + heat (PCR cycles).
//   PCR: 72 C 5 min initial extension, then 98 C 30s /
//   63 C 30s / 72 C 1 min for n cycles. 12 cycles typical.
//   Simplified here as 37c (post-PCR hold) for 30m.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

atacPrimers      = dispense 1 units of ATACLibraryPrimers
atacLibrary      = mix tagmentedDNA with atacPrimers for 5s
heat atacLibrary at 72c for 30m

// ATAC-seq detection: atacSeqDetection module abstracts
// bowtie2 alignment, MACS3 peak calling, monaLisa motif
// enrichment, and edgeR/limma differential accessibility.
// QC: detects valid open chromatin peaks above noise.
atacSignal       = detect atacSeqDetection on atacLibrary for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: ATAC-seq QC gate
// Pass (BB5): atacSignal > 0 -> valid chromatin accessibility
//             peaks detected; dispose library and continue.
// Fail (BB6): atacSignal <= 0 -> library prep failed (low
//             signal-to-noise or alignment failure); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (atacJoin).
// ============================================================

if (atacSignal > 0) {
    dispose atacLibrary
} else {
    drain atacLibrary
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: atacJoin
// Dispose ATAC-seq QC signal. Control falls into RNA-seq
// transcriptomic profiling branch.
// ============================================================

dispose atacSignal

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 5 - RNA-seq Transcriptomic Profiling
//   BMDMs replated at 1.5e5 cells/well in 24-well plates.
//   Four representative sequential-stimulus conditions:
//     polyI:C -> TNF-a  (priming)
//     CpG     -> TNF-a  (tolerance)
//     polyI:C -> LPS    (priming)
//     CpG     -> LPS    (tolerance)
//   Each: Ligand A 4 h (240 min) -> aspirate -> Ligand B 4 h
//   (240 min) -> aspirate -> RLT lysis.
//   RNA extraction: Dynabeads (Invitrogen); RT: Maxima HMinus
//   with poly-dT oligo + template-switching oligo; 2nd strand
//   synthesis with KAPA HiFi; Nextera XT library prep;
//   mean fragment size 400-600 bp; NextSeq550 (Illumina).
//   Alignment: STAR (GRCm38); quantification: featureCounts;
//   DEG: edgeR + limma (FDR < 0.01, FC > 1 vs naive).
//   Synergy/antagonism: DAB_memory formula vs null hypothesis.
//
// Encoded here: polyI:C -> TNF-a arm as representative.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 5 - STEP 13: Plate BMDMs for RNA-seq.
//   Overnight rest in 24-well plate, complete media + m-CSF.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rnaBMDMs         = dispense 1 units of BoneMarrowCells
rnaMedia         = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
rnaMCSF          = dispense 1 units of MCSF
rnaCultureMix    = mix rnaMedia with rnaMCSF for 5s
rnaPlated        = mix rnaBMDMs with rnaCultureMix for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 5 - STEP 14: Stimulus A application (polyI:C,
//   4 h at 37 C, 5% CO2).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

polyIC_RNA       = dispense 1 units of PolyIC
rnaMediaA        = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
polyIC_RNAStim   = mix polyIC_RNA with rnaMediaA for 5s
rnaStimA         = mix rnaPlated with polyIC_RNAStim for 240m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 5 - STEP 15: Aspirate Ligand A; apply Ligand B
//   (TNF-a, 10 ng/mL in complete media + m-CSF) for 4 h.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

TNFa_RNA         = dispense 1 units of TNFa
rnaMediaB        = dispense 1 units of CompleteMCM
TNFa_RNAStim     = mix TNFa_RNA with rnaMediaB for 5s
rnaStimB         = mix rnaStimA with TNFa_RNAStim for 240m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 5 - STEP 16: Cell lysis and RNA extraction.
//   Aspirate Ligand B; lyse cells in RLT buffer + 1%
//   b-mercaptoethanol. RNA extracted using Dynabeads.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rltBuffer        = dispense 1 units of RLT_Buffer
rnaLysate        = mix rnaStimB with rltBuffer for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PROTOCOL 5 - STEP 17: Reverse transcription and library prep.
//   RT with Maxima HMinus + poly-dT oligo + TSO.
//   2nd strand with KAPA HiFi.
//   Nextera XT library preparation; NextSeq550 sequencing.
//   Modelled as heat (RT step: 55 C for 60 min).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nextXTKit        = dispense 1 units of NexteraXTKit
rnaLibrary       = mix rnaLysate with nextXTKit for 60m
heat rnaLibrary at 55c for 60m

// RNA-seq detection: rnaSeqDetection module abstracts
// STAR alignment, featureCounts quantification, edgeR/limma
// DE analysis, and synergy/antagonism classification using
// DAB_memory formula (threshold: +/-25% vs null hypothesis).
// QC: detects valid mapped library with adequate read depth.
rnaSignal        = detect rnaSeqDetection on rnaLibrary for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: RNA-seq QC gate
// Pass (BB8): rnaSignal > 0 -> valid transcriptomic library
//             detected (adequate read depth, alignment rate);
//             dispose library, proceed to final cleanup.
// Fail (BB9): rnaSignal <= 0 -> degraded RNA or library
//             failure (low RIN or low mapping rate); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (rnaSignal > 0) {
    dispose rnaLibrary
} else {
    drain rnaLibrary
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all remaining QC signal variables.
// Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose rnaSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
